{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517020-what-do-brujah-mean-to-you","id":1517020,"title":"What do [Brujah] Mean To You?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-02T18:26:27-07:00","id":1517020,"title":"What do [Brujah] Mean To You?","content":"This is the first thread in what might become a series of threads called \u2018What does X mean to you?\u2019, if people seem interested.<br /> <br /> The inspiration for this thread is two fold: one, as many of you probably know, I like to go on somewhat long and hopefully interesting or useful diatribes about themes and vibes in the World of Darkness setting, and I\u2019m always interested in what others have to say in the same vein. The other inspiration is something I read X5 threads for (in part anyway): the way that those threads seem to uniquely draw people into discussing what they feel parts of the setting/game \u2018ought\u2019 to be and I\u2019m always fascinated by the spectrum of ideas that people have and I often find them very exciting and interesting. So a part of this thread comes from the hopes that people will bring some of that energy to the discussion.<br /> <br /> That being said, I\u2019ll start with Clan Brujah, first of the OG 7 clans and, I must be honest, one of my favorite since the first time I opened VtM.<br /> <br /> * * * * * * *<br /> <br /> What are the Brujah?<br /> <br /> The Brujah are vampires in VTM that are designed to embody certain archetypes. They are more humanistic vampires like the Toreador &amp; Ventrue (the Brujah to me have always had a feeling akin to Spike from Buffy, Lestat from the Vampire Chronicles [More his depiction from Louis\u2019 perspective/the rock star thing], &amp; the Lost Boys). The Brujah are the leather jacket wearing punk rock vampires of the 1970s &amp; 1980s; bred on urban decay chic, insatiable passion, rebellion, hard &amp; raw music, radical politics, and the general punk attitude. They move fast, hit hard, and are rock stars; and barely beneath the surface is a roiling, murderous rage. <br /> <br /> Of course, that\u2019s not all the Brujah are or became:<br /> <br /> \u2022The Brujah became the vampire tag-line for unorthodoxy and rebellion: they are the loyal opposition of the Camarilla (and I imagine many of the Ivory Tower\u2019s originally radical ideas were cooked up by ancillae &amp; elder Brujah), they are one of the principle clans of the Sabbat (leading Founders and alongside the Ventrue &amp; certain Lasombra are probably the Vanguard of the Loyalist faction), and throughout VtM history Brujah has basically been a byword for Anarch<br /> <br /> \u2022The Brujah have a defining quality in a generational divide: one which may be caused by degeneration of the blood or natural laws. Older Brujah become carefully regimented, emulating the Philosopher Kings &amp; Prometheans of Old Carthage, while the Younger Brujah are more typically iconoclasts and rabble with red-hot blood (and Ancillae Individualists somewhere in the middle). Whether this is in fact the degeneration of Brujah\u2019s blood under the Curse of Troile, a natural consequence of vampiric survival mechanisms over time, or some combination; I leave to each their own<br /> <br /> \u2022The Brujah have become inseparably associated with the concept of Carthage in VtM, however part of me wonders if that isn\u2019t missing the forest for the trees somewhat. I can see Carthage as being not only a Brujah project but a Assamite or Lasombra project. What seems more in keeping with me is that Carthage is one part of a larger Brujah pattern: a tendency towards Promethean ideals (alongside the Assamites) as well as antagonistic projects against rivals such as the Ventrue (alongside the Lasombra, to a point). In this view I imagine in Dark Ages for example we have a spectrum of Brujah. Brujah of Mesopotamia who from the beginning were deeply interwoven with each state and their competitions (perhaps with Assyrian Brujah Charioteers running wild later on). Brujah of Athens conducting political experiments while the Ventrue organize Sparta and the Toreador orchestrate Hellenic culture from old Crete. Brujah would indeed be in Carthage but they would also be at the heart of Rome challenging the Ventrue &amp; the Senate from within, not to mention in the forests of Gaul and Germania. Later you would still have Brujah everywhere - in Spain alongside the Lasombra to plague Ventrue England &amp; Toreador France, in Anatolia for Brujah &amp; Assamite Ottomons to terrorize Ventrue &amp; Tremere Austria Hapsburg Ventrue, and Brujah everywhere within as well, etc.<br /> <br /> \u2022I\u2019ve never been able to settle on which specifics of the Ilyes &amp; Troile story I like best and I\u2019m okay with that. I suppose my sketch would be Ilyes as an antediluvian chosen to be a warrior-king philosopher type (akin to Haqim somewhat, but with a less focused vision). Troile was their counterpart, the antithesis to their thesis and an important part of Brujah\u2019s process. Whether Troile was an imaginary interlocutor, a priestess, a lover, a prophet; I don\u2019t know. Regardless the two were inevitably linked. As time went on they grew alienated from one another, perhaps with Troile suspicious of the sources Ilyes found to develop their Temporis (likely a Lilian source) and this would eventually culminate in shadow boxing around the Trojan War where in the profanation of the city the two forces made contact again and we are still seeing the development of their constant dialectical struggle. Whatever comes from the struggle has yet to be born in full, but the conflict of development generates the energy of the clan. The Brujah Founder is likely buried somewhere below ancient Carthage (or perhaps Troy) but while sleeping their effect is still felt. They are torn within themselves over their goal for Gehenna and the Jyhad. They use the Spirit of their Presence to contest their kin but what are their own goals? Ilyes perhaps hoped to use Lilian Gnosticism to transcend temporal bonds and overcome the Jyhad &amp; Gehenna that way and perhaps Troile hoped to use Promethean means to establish the Third City and either erect a throne for the Dark Father to preempt Gehenna or to create a Work of such greatness as to render Gehenna unnecessary - an earthly paradise, a Promethean Republic of The Philosopher King/Queen Brujah. The struggle of these impulses may still be felt in the Jyhad of Brujah. On one hand seeking philosophical truths which transcend the limits of reality and on the other hand the philosophical truths to perfect reality.<br /> <br /> \u2022Speaking of the Jyhad, a part of me has always wanted to come up with a few methuselah characters for each clan who I can use as figures in the global Jyhad to better understand what ripples of intrigue may be going on. For Brujah I imagine that a few good characters for that would be one in North Africa/West Asia (an old Carthaginian) and perhaps one either to represent Greece or Spain and be a Promethean in the \u2018modern\u2019 Camarilla sense (perhaps the ultimate backer of the Brujah Founder of the Camarilla). Of course for North America we have Menele who we can use as the representative of Brujah at the highest levels of the Jyhad in the Americas - still tangling with Helene in his sleep and extending his influence to keep the Anarch Movement a viable challenge to any pockets of Helene\u2019s control while grooming his preferred philosopher-princes/barons to eventually arise as Napoleonic/Caesarian figures from the struggle.<br /> <br /> \u2022For the Camarilla I view the Brujah as fulfilling the role of Loyal Opposition at every level. The Elders are the Ideologues who helped define the various ideological camps of the sect - from Princely Prerogative to Radical Conclavism. The Elders have a somewhat softer than average approach to dissent; viewing it as a crucible for truly great ancillae (and some probably having some level of secret respect for their kin who became leaders of the Sabbat or Anarchs). That said a hardline Brujah Elder will typically be more hardline than any other Elder, whatever that line is. Brujah Elders will likely have a unique web of policies and ideas they apply to the sect and its government, becoming either supporters or opponents of local princes based on those points. Brujah Ancillae, as their elder counterparts imagine, are the crucible for development in the sect - when allowed. Brujah Ancillae can be some of the most volatile when unable to gain purchase, often forming a vanguard of Reform-Anarch programs; not radical Anarchs but Anarchs who would be Prince and carry out their own reforms. This energy can be useful if one has it in a retainer or if it\u2019s satisfied by the position of Harpy or Sheriff, but if not it\u2019s a double edged sword. Neonate Brujah in the Camarilla are a spectrum. Most are probably Anarch sympathizers to some degree. Most probably are Iconoclasts or Iconoclast curious (if only by temperament and not ideology). Most will not survive and those who do will find their own camps where they can settle as rock stars and cult leaders amongst humanity. The relatively large number and volatility of Brujah Neonates makes them a double edged sword in any domain - great shock troops, but that could be good or bad.<br /> <br /> \u2022Brujah in the Sabbat, I feel, have always gotten the short shrift. Brujah were incredibly prominent in the Anarch Revolts and I\u2019d be surprised if, like the Anarchs of today, they didn\u2019t make up a plurality. That said, with the focus on the Status Quo &amp; Conservative factions I can understand the focus on Lasombra &amp; Tzimisce but I\u2019ve always felt, like in the Camarilla, the Brujah Antitribu should be well represented amongst the loyal opposition of Sabbat Politics as well with members of high standing. That said the lion\u2019s share are probably still more with the Loyalists than anything else.<br /> <br /> \u2022The Brujah and the Anarchs are practically synonymous. Rob Leeland, Tyler, Jeremy MacNeil, Salvador Garcia, etc. It\u2019s a classic for a reason. From the numerous Brujah in every generation of Anarchs (from the peasants of the first revolt, to the liberal radicals of the French Revolution, the radicals of the 19th century, and the socialists of the 20th century) with both the Brujah Council of the USSR &amp; the California Free State having major influences from Brujah. Hell, it\u2019s been a long-running joke for a reason that the Brujah are basically the Ventrue of the Anarchs (or the Lasombra of the Anarchs, if you prefer). This is true and I do think it\u2019s interesting. While I don\u2019t think it should distract from the sincerity of many Anarchs and the reasons why Brujah would naturally predominate, it is also probably not untrue that, just as Toreador &amp; Ventrue elders supported the Camarilla to advance themselves post-War of Princes and the Lasombra &amp; Tzimisce supported the Sabbat, the Brujah elders supported the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> These are all the things that came to mind for me, off the top of my head, and while it\u2019s by no means comprehensive I hope that it was interesting to some of you who read and that you\u2019d be interested in adding something to the thread and sharing your own thoughts.<br /> <br /> Thanks for reading!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T02:05:13-07:00","id":1517042,"title":"","content":"Personally I've always found the Brujah a bit of a joke as written. Individually formidable but collectively inept. Part of the problem is the writters tendancy to romanticise dissidence and idealism without really engaging with it and trying to keep the setting relentlessly pessimistic.<br /> <br /> Part of it is probably because I started out as a dark age player and my first pc was a brujah philisopher king and my own heavy involvement in left wing politixs irl. so my bias' show","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T03:12:33-07:00","id":1517048,"title":"","content":"Interesting thread and first post. The title initially threw me off-guard and I thought this was about the Antediluvian and not the Clan.<br /> <br /> What I think that the Brujah means to me is partly passion, for whatever that cause might be, as well as human society bleeding over into Cainite existance. The last being a theme they share with the Toreador but in a different way.<br /> <br /> What I could add is that to me the Brujah don't necessarily only embody left-wing passion for freedom and justice but can be passionate about much more sinister or directly malicious ideas or concepts. As well as the risk of them degenerating into mere brutes, or surrendering intellectual activity to enforcement of their wants by violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T08:46:05-07:00","id":1517073,"title":"","content":"Brujah to me means is we have a clan who greatest strength is also there downfall which is there passion to change how society works and make it more equal in there eyes which leads to the conflict as they are not the most organized clans out there and will get in each others way much to the amusement of the Ventrue or Lasombra clans.<br /> <br /> In others words like what my Malkavian character said they can gain power quickly and lose it even more quickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T12:38:13-07:00","id":1517090,"title":"","content":"95% Radicals of all ideologies.<br /> <br /> 5% People full of passion and wisdom.<br /> <br /> Also the most numerous group of vampires. Personally I love them as I use the carthian movement instead of the Anarchs to represent different ideologies applied to the vampiric society and the Brujah help with that. I also use them to parady different radicals and subcultures becase the Brujah tend to take everything up to eleven. They are a beutiful narrative tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T13:31:20-07:00","id":1517095,"title":"","content":"It means having every square inch of your existence defined by rage, which is exhausting. Brujah sort of live in perpetual flight or fight mode, except there's no flight option.<br /> <br /> The fledgling stage acts as a filter as the newborns drop like flies; most will fail to get ahold of themselves and get put down as rabid dogs, while many will off themselves because they can't cope with the emotional pain and exhaustion of living in constant hate and anger. A few of the unstable disasters survive into the neonate stage outside of the Cam, but they're still liable to burn bright and fast before they piss off somebody bigger than them (be they kindred, hunters or worse...). If you survive for any meaningful length of time, then you're one of the ones with damned good self-control. Brujah tend to be introspective and proactive as a necessity; they watch what they think and feel closely, identify things that help calm them and things that have the opposite effect, and try to shape their environment appropriately. They're driven to identify problems, causes and ponder solutions as a means of survival, lending to their reputation as philosophers... also adding to this is their tendency to hate each other and feud over it for having the wrong opinions, \u00e0 la Diogenes and Plato but nastier.<br /> Not all of them are &quot;activists&quot;, but even so, they'll often go out of their way to try and tailor the society they live in to their comfort, surround themselves with the &quot;right people&quot;, and decompress by directing their anger in &quot;appropriate&quot; directions at people who &quot;deserve it&quot;.<br /> <br /> If the environment is your hot button, you might engage in eco-terrorism. If you think women outside of the role of homemakers and mothers is unnatural or ungodly or whatever, you may go out of your way to abuse and humiliate women who don't fit your ideal of what they should be, or ghoul them and force them into that mold for their own good. If you think [insert group here] is causing the downfall of modern society you may go out of your way to exclusively feed on (and probably kill) people of that group. Eat the Rich is a slogan one might take literally.<br /> You might even be utterly indiferent to political issues and social divisions... but things such as people with poor manners, or having to take orders from others, may trigger homicide ideation.<br /> <br /> Contrary to the Anarch stereotype, the clan isn't always loud about their venting. Yes, some go out of their way to break shit; others go in for being authoritarian nightmares who are only hurting you because they care and are trying to &quot;save you from yourself/ves&quot;; some channel it into emotional abuse and bullying.\u200b<br /> <br /> In the end the rage in their blood always overwhelms them; they can't help destroying what they build. Relationships, alliances, your reputation, prized/vital possessions... accidents will happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T13:37:11-07:00","id":1517096,"title":"","content":"5% might be to high of a number for a wise Brujah Leondro16 for what we seen in the lore thus far on the clan at all. Brujah like Critias, Menela, Damian and even Bell seem to be a much smaller minority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-06-2023, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T14:08:00-07:00","id":1517099,"title":"","content":"A friend of mine said the Brujah made sense to him once he realized, &quot;You should always play the Brujah as angry but the reason they're angry is because the world fucking sucks.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T15:20:19-07:00","id":1517109,"title":"","content":"I see them as a clan that wants to remake society, but don't understand the naivety and cost behind it. A clan that seems unable, or unwilling, to learn from its own mistakes, and is incapable of learning from both the successes and failures of others. A clan that seems to make everything worse.<br /> <br /> Just look at Cartage, the Soviet Union, and California.<br /> <br /> Cartage, a paradise praised by the brujah, was in actuality a hellhole. <b>Eshmunamash </b>a fifth-gen brujah who was a doctor and actually lived in Carthage at the time, was a firsthand witness of the human sacrifices and the Baali infestation, and when he went to Troile to report this, Troile promised to look into it, but never did. He got so disgusted that he went to Rome and informed Camilla of the defenses around Carthage and other vital information.<br /> <br /> The Brujah Council were directly involved with the Soviet Union and actually supported Stalin. They legitimately thought that Stalin was the best guy to lead it, and preferred him over Trotsky. They also intentionally ignored the millions of innocents that died under Stalin's reign, all while thinking everything was going to work out in the end.<br /> <br /> And that's before we get into California. An Anarch free state, where anarchy is enforced. Gangs pretty much roam the streets, and for the most part, are free to do what they want. There is little to no neutral grounds, and if I remember correctly, the second anarch source book goes into how much of an idiot Jeremy MacNeil is for his hand in creating it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T18:57:35-07:00","id":1517127,"title":"","content":"The big thing to remember is that for Brujah as a clan, politics -- <i>any</i> politics -- are means to an end. That end being delusion, making believe they're anything but violent bullies driven by their Beasts. The only thing they care about politically, is how violent a given ideology already is, how easily it can be driven to violence, and how well it justifies violence, because that facade lets them lie to themselves that it's not about the violence. All vampires are corruptive, parasitic monsters, and Brujah are no different: they corrupt and parasitize ideologies and movements, and move onto the next best thing when the lies they tell themselves wear thin.<br /> <br /> Not exclusively physical violence, although that's the basest and most common form of it, and at what they excel. Verbal violence, emotional violence, psychological violence, cultural or economic violence, it's all on the table for Brujah. Destroy, destroy, destroy, but pretend it's for some higher purpose so you can sleep during the day.<br /> <br /> Some -- usually the naive or just plain stupid -- actually believe it. Then they die, or grow out of it. But mostly, they die.<br /> <br /> The followers of Entelechy just try to deny it altogether, and replace lies about violence for a higher purpose with lies about Kumbaya drum circles being the secret solution to pretending you're something you're not. Works about as well as a fishnet condom. Brujah <i>antitribu</i> just decided to be honest with themselves, and we see what Brujah think of Brujah who are honest with themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 07-03-2023, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T20:19:55-07:00","id":1517189,"title":"","content":"I see them as a clan that wants to remake society, but don't understand the naivety and cost behind it. A clan that seems unable, or unwilling, to learn from its own mistakes, and is incapable of learning from both the successes and failures of others. A clan that seems to make everything worse.<br /> <br /> Just look at Cartage, the Soviet Union, and California.<br /> <br /> Cartage, a paradise praised by the brujah, was in actuality a hellhole. <b>Eshmunamash </b>a fifth-gen brujah who was a doctor and actually lived in Carthage at the time, was a firsthand witness of the human sacrifices and the Baali infestation, and when he went to Troile to report this, Troile promised to look into it, but never did. He got so disgusted that he went to Rome and informed Camilla of the defenses around Carthage and other vital information.<br /> <br /> The Brujah Council were directly involved with the Soviet Union and actually supported Stalin. They legitimately thought that Stalin was the best guy to lead it, and preferred him over Trotsky. They also intentionally ignored the millions of innocents that died under Stalin's reign, all while thinking everything was going to work out in the end.<br /> <br /> And that's before we get into California. An Anarch free state, where anarchy is enforced. Gangs pretty much roam the streets, and for the most part, are free to do what they want. There is little to no neutral grounds, and if I remember correctly, the second anarch source book goes into how much of an idiot Jeremy MacNeil is for his hand in creating it.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T20:34:13-07:00","id":1517192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517020-what-do-brujah-mean-to-you?p=1517189#post1517189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see them as a clan that wants to remake society, but don't understand the naivety and cost behind it. A clan that seems unable, or unwilling, to learn from its own mistakes, and is incapable of learning from both the successes and failures of others. A clan that seems to make everything worse.<br /> <br /> Just look at Cartage, the Soviet Union, and California.<br /> <br /> Cartage, a paradise praised by the brujah, was in actuality a hellhole. <b>Eshmunamash </b>a fifth-gen brujah who was a doctor and actually lived in Carthage at the time, was a firsthand witness of the human sacrifices and the Baali infestation, and when he went to Troile to report this, Troile promised to look into it, but never did. He got so disgusted that he went to Rome and informed Camilla of the defenses around Carthage and other vital information.<br /> <br /> The Brujah Council were directly involved with the Soviet Union and actually supported Stalin. They legitimately thought that Stalin was the best guy to lead it, and preferred him over Trotsky. They also intentionally ignored the millions of innocents that died under Stalin's reign, all while thinking everything was going to work out in the end.<br /> <br /> And that's before we get into California. An Anarch free state, where anarchy is enforced. Gangs pretty much roam the streets, and for the most part, are free to do what they want. There is little to no neutral grounds, and if I remember correctly, the second anarch source book goes into how much of an idiot Jeremy MacNeil is for his hand in creating it.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I always note that vampire depictions of things are decidedly slanted and never take anything at face value.<br /> <br /> Specifically, my view of certain paradises need to remember that Brujah may be idealistic but they are VAMPIRES.<br /> <br /> 1. The Soviet Union was the alternative to the Camarilla and the Brujah were on top of that one. The most powerful nation on Earth but for one other and established based around their Clan. Yes, they couldn't control Stalin (The NWO couldn't either) but the only people that suffered were humans.<br /> <br /> 2. I interpret Jeremy MacNeil as actually having the Anarch Free States function EXACTLY how it was intended. It's a survival of the fittest free for all. If you can't get along, you get out.<br /> <br /> Vampires are now feuding clans and that's exactly how he wanted his New Scotland.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-04-2023, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T22:55:31-07:00","id":1517196,"title":"","content":"They are in a sense, catalists of change. Good intentions and naviet\u00e9 paired with superior ego eg. what we belive is good is the right way always leads to change and more often than not, catastrophes.<br /> They are not unlike Lucifer<br /> Interesting to mention, the so-called &quot;Brujah's opposition&quot; to the status quo and awareness of its cruelties frequently led them to the conclusion that, if those claiming to be good are actually evil, perhaps those labeled as evil may actually be good...<br /> Maybe this is why many Brujah were instrumental in the creation of the many varieties of the Road of Sin. One variant, the Road of the Adversary, does actually emulate Lucifer as symbol of freedom and rebellion against tyranny, and the traditional Promethean path of the Clan similarly holds great admiration for Prometheus as another rebellious lightbringer.<br /> While often rude, noisy and very unruly, they are very passionate individuals and are on par with the Toreador when it comes to try to understand the human world... but for one reason or another, maybe becasue the vampiric ego, the elusive meaning and real understanding evade their grasp and everything crumbles around them for this very reason<br /> So if there is a word, one word that describes what the Brujah &quot;mean to me&quot; or describes them?<br /> That would would be: Lucifer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T19:27:07-07:00","id":1517621,"title":"","content":"&quot;Brujah-Hahaha, Brujah-Hahaha&quot;. That's my take; I didn't see anything else in them other than what the fellow players would chant. I do, however, like the Requiem version of the Brujah, a bit, though, I want to smack them and tell them they're vampires, for Christ's sake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T21:56:39-07:00","id":1517625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517020-what-do-brujah-mean-to-you?p=1517621#post1517621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Brujah-Hahaha, Brujah-Hahaha&quot;. That's my take; I didn't see anything else in them other than what the fellow players would chant. I do, however, like the Requiem version of the Brujah, a bit, though, I want to smack them and tell them they're vampires, for Christ's sake.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the problem with Brujah?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T19:33:18-07:00","id":1517669,"title":"","content":"As a person with problems of rage and love for politics, the Brujah means a lot to me and are my favorite clan. People dont understand what is to have real anger problems. You are <b>ALL THE TIME FIGHTING IT</b>. You are trying to stay in a chill state of the mind, or trying to control yourself. You have fear of hurting the people that you love. You cant just shut it down. Every moment of your existence is this fight against your mind, against the thought of trying to break everything. And you try to cling to something. Something in which you can focus your energy on. Politics, most normally, end up being that. Because the world around you is shit, and you are fucking mad about it. You hate that nobody want to change the world. The world need fire. You can be the fire. You become the fire, because, well, you were fire in the first place, but now you can at least try to do something with that. You have ideals, and passion, and fire, because is the only way to stay sane. At least, you dont have the fear of it ending up consuming the ones you love. But you can end up consuming you. You fight against a cruel and stupid and unjust world, and that anger you more. Why nobody fight with me? Why nobody see that everything is shit? How somebody can defend this system, or other that i hate the same? You become more angered. Sometimes, you cross a mental line. Maybe you start acting with political violence. Maybe you start preaching more radical politics. Maybe, you consume yourself. In the best case, you consume yourself hitting some of that motherfuckers that CAN UNDERSTAND THE FUCKING POINT. MAYBE THAT IS HOW THEY CAN UNDERSTAND. Fight to the end. Or maybe you consume yourself alone. Every bit of your mind, your body, being anger. Maybe you are not in this stage. But the Anger. You cant stop it. YOU. CANT. STOP. THE. ANGER. This is being a Brujah. A constant cicle of fear, self loathing, anger, and burning your mind, body and soul. But hey, you have the eternity. Just try to not burn yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28021-camaradadoppio","name":"CamaradaDoppio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28021_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T19:11:56-07:00","id":1517727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517020-what-do-brujah-mean-to-you?p=1517625#post1517625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's the problem with Brujah?</div> </div> </div> </div>In NWoD, they're a fairly new branch of the Grangrel-family that are basically bikers, with fangs. They act like biker-thugs, and not like immortal creatures of the night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T01:27:20-07:00","id":1517744,"title":"","content":"Its odd how the requiem tool the least interesting part of the brujah and ran with that considering what they did with the nosferatu and ventrue","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T03:42:24-07:00","id":1522448,"title":"","content":"Well, I see them as trailblazers. Some trails go straight to hell, some are duds, and some make meaningful changes, but they're opening new paths to vampiredom with reckless abandon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T17:14:23-07:00","id":1522543,"title":"","content":"Brujah still means Damsel, Nines, and Smiling Jack to me. Most of my favorite characters are Brujah, I really like their discipline spread it kinda gives bad ass rockerboy vibes, and their clan flaw and how it makes them passionate to the point of violence is something I have always found really cool. Their history what with the fall of carthage and being the black sheep of the high clans is another interesting angle.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T15:02:47-07:00","id":1522602,"title":"","content":"A disorganized clan with differing ideas on how to make a more equalitian society and spend more time warring with each other then they do against the Ventrue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T15:56:28-07:00","id":1522606,"title":"","content":"In my opinion, the Brujah feel an even pathological need to fight for an ideology, however distorted it may be, even those that preach only violence. They simply have a need to fight, the Sabbat are only those who are sincere with this desire and the lack of human morality makes them stop looking for excuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-15T15:36:31-07:00","id":1522647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517020-what-do-brujah-mean-to-you?p=1522606#post1522606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, the Brujah feel an even pathological need to fight for an ideology, however distorted it may be, even those that preach only violence. They simply have a need to fight, the Sabbat are only those who are sincere with this desire and the lack of human morality makes them stop looking for excuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a fair point about the Brujah needing a cause to fight for even if the cause is scary or has shown to be a failure over and over. I mean lets take a look at the Brujah Dominic who was embraced in the city-state and how he still holds onto his grudge against the Ventrue's clan role in the fall of Carthage and will target major clan figures that were born and embraced hundreds of years after the fact as the ones who did the heavy lifting so to speak have suffered final death or gone deep into topor or into solitude. <br /> <br /> That is a long time to hold onto a grudge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-16-2023, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T03:37:32-07:00","id":1536973,"title":"","content":"They are intended to originally be Warrior Philosophers, who fell from grace, and are now mostly brutes who hate authority. And I can sympathize with that. Maybe 